<p>"If you have never wept bitter tears because a wonderful story has come to an end and you must take your leave of the characters 
with whom you have shared so many adventures, whom you have loved and admired, for whom you have hoped and feared, and without whose company 
life seems empty and meaningless. If such things have not been part of your own experience, you probably won't understand..." 
<br>
- Michael Ende, The Neverending Story
</p>
